jobs.description:
Are you ready to make an impact in one of the largest warehouses in the Benelux? In this role, you will work at a brand-new, large-scale site that is currently undergoing significant development. The operation is growing rapidly, many new colleagues are joining, and processes are being further built and refined. This requires strong supervisors who can bring structure, direction, and clarity to the operation.

As a Warehouse Supervisor, you are the key link between the team leaders on the floor and the warehouse manager. You will indirectly lead a large group of employees and ensure that daily operations run smoothly, efficiently, and according to agreed standards. You will work in an environment where structure is essential and processes must be strictly followed from A to Z. At the same time, you are the one who maintains oversight, makes adjustments, and takes decisions when necessary.

Your responsibilities:

- Leading and supporting multiple team leaders and their teams;
- Monitoring daily operations, planning, and performance;
- Conducting conversations regarding absenteeism, performance, and employee development;
- Justifying operational decisions towards warehouse management (such as capacity and overtime);
- Ensuring strict adherence to processes and procedures;
- Monitoring KPIs, quality, and operational progress;
- Coordinating with different departments and internal stakeholders;
- Identifying bottlenecks and implementing improvements ;
- Working with reports and administrative processes (including Excel).

For this position, we are looking for a strong and experienced supervisor who is used to working in a high-paced, operational warehouse environment.

- Minimum of 3 years’ experience in a leadership role within a logistics or warehouse environment. Experience in retail or supermarkets is not considered relevant for this role;
- Fluent in English (required);
- Experience with Excel and reporting;
- Available full-time (40 hours per week) in a 2-shi

As a Forklift and/or Reach Truck Operator, you are responsible for keeping the warehouse and shipping process running efficiently. Your daily tasks include collecting and moving goods, scanning shipments, checking orders for accuracy, loading and unloading trucks, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

You will work full-time (40 hours per week) in a fixed team at the Moerdijk warehouse and are willing to work in a two-shift schedule.

- Valid Forklift and/or Reach Truck certificate;
- At least 1 year of experience operating a forklift or reach truck;
- Full-time availability (40 hours per week) willing to work a fixed two-shift schedule (06:00 - 15:00, 07:00 - 16:00, 08:00 - 17:00, or 15:00 - 00:00);
- Own transportation and willingness to work in Moerdijk;
- You are at least 18 years old and a VMBO or MBO working thinking level (or equivalent);
- You have a good command of the English language;
- Accurate, safety-conscious, and a team player;

What will you do?

Do you have an affinity for technology or experience in technical production, and are you handy with practical work? Are you also looking for a long-term job opportunity? Then look no further!

As a Field Service Technician, you will visit various organizations, ranging from large government institutions and universities to hospitals. The work requires specialized skills, for which you will receive internal training.

Your responsibilities include:

- Maintenance and renovation of air handling systems;
- Cleaning and gas-free preparation of installations within the chemical industry;
- Collaborating with various clients to ensure technical installations function optimally.

Who are you?

In addition to an interest in technology and technical insight, you have:

- A VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- A valid Category B driving license;
- Strong communication skills, customer friendliness, and initiative;
- Good command of the English and/or Dutch language.

Are you looking for a varied role in production? Do you enjoy taking responsibility and working as part of a team? If this sounds like you, then the role of Production Worker at Klaas Puul is perfect for you! Working for an organization that is recognized for its success? KP is one of the finalists in the North Holland Entrepreneur Awards 2026, a great recognition of our ambition, innovation, and entrepreneurial culture.



 Please note: only candidates who are currently living in the Netherlands can apply.

In this role, you will be involved in a variety of activities across logistics, production, and cleaning. You may assist with packaging our shrimp and other tasks that help maintain an efficient production process. Hygiene and safety are top priorities for us, and you will ensure that your work always meets these standards.



You will work a fixed shift of your choice:

  - Morning/Afternoon Shift: 6:00 AM – 2:30 PM

OR

  - Afternoon/Evening Shift: 2:30 PM – 10:30 PM

What you bring:

At Klaas Puul, we are looking for colleagues who fit into our growing company. You are ready to take on challenges with us and contribute to developing a new, shared company culture. You bring certain experience and skills that you can apply in this role:

  - MBO-level (intermediate vocational education) work and thinking skills;

  - 0–2 years of relevant work experience, preferably in a production or logistics environment;

  - You must live in the Netherlands; applications from abroad will not be considered;

  - Proactive, hygienic, precise, and a true team player;

  - Good verbal and written communication skills in English; Dutch is a plus;

  - Forklift certification is a plus;

  - Basic knowledge of food safety and familiarity with guidelines around food fraud and food defense, or a willingness to develop these skills further.

What we offer:

At Klaas Puul, you will work in an informal, dynamic environment with plenty of freedom and opportunities

Doing a job right in your own neighborhood where you can have friendly chats with the locals? How great is that?!✨ You can make it happen as a flyer delivery driver at Spotta in Amsterdam! This job takes about 2 to a maximum of 4 hours per week. You don't have to travel, and you are truly flexible in deciding when you deliver the flyers. On top of that, you earn €16.19 per hour (incl. holiday pay)!💸 Curious to learn more? Read on below!👇

What we offer
- A great wage of €16.19 per hour!
- Healthy: stay physically active in the fresh air!
- Work in your own neighborhood—zero commute time!
- A flexible job—you choose when you deliver!
- Hit the road fully equipped with handy Spotta bags
- A flexible job of 2-4 hours

Who you are
As a flyer delivery driver at Spotta in Amsterdam, it is important that you can work independently. You are also responsible and reliable—ensuring the flyers are always delivered neatly and on time. Furthermore, you:

- Live in the postal code area 1051 until 1059 + 1071 until 1083 in Amsterdam;
- Are available to work 2 to a maximum of 4 hours per week;
- Are able to deliver the flyers on Friday, Saturday, Sunday, or Monday (you choose when);
- Are physically capable of lifting flyer bundles and walking or cycling;
- Speak Dutch or English;
- Are comfortable receiving the flyer delivery packages at your home;
- Own a bicycle with a rear luggage rack (required for the panniers).

What will you do
As a flyer delivery driver at Spotta, you will deliver flyer bundles in a neighborhood. On Thursday, Friday, or Saturday, the flyers you need to deliver will be dropped off at your house. You don't have to stay home for this, but it is important that the packages remain secure. You have until Monday at 7:00 PM to finish your deliveries. Ideal, because you can schedule it exactly around your availability (and keep an eye on the weather forecast!).

